# Pending deletion belongs to the checkout

Two live sessions sharing a checkout share one persisted deletion selection.

Attach `alpha/first` and `alpha/alias` to the same named `feature` workspace.
Filter to `first` and stage it: the footer should count both sessions, including
the hidden alias, while only one marker file is written to their shared checkout.

    :b jj tmux cat sh test sleep (available)
    :cp tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ jj git init alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --base alpha --create feature (exit: 0)

```stdout
alpha/feature
```

The CLI reuses one live session per checkout. Rename it and attach a second
alias manually to construct the shared-checkout state this case needs.

    :t rename-session -t alpha/feature alpha/first (success)
    :t new-session -d -s alpha/alias -c alpha.feature "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=alpha/alias:' @smth.repo '#{pane_start_path}' (success)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth -r 'alpha*'; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 12 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :k C-p first
    :settle -d 2s -e '1/5' -e alpha/first -e 'C-d. delete' (settled)
    :k C-d
    :snap -d 2s -e '2 sessions' -e '1 hidden'

```terminal
session: first                                                                                                         ┃
  1/5 | [C-r] repo: none                                                                                               ┃
   first                                    ~/first                                                               repo ┃
   first                                                                                                          tmux ┃
▌× alpha/first                              ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] unstage, [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                 delete [C-y] 2 sessions (1 hidden) [C-g] cancel┃
```

    :$ test -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

Both rows are staged, and the footer counts two sessions, with no hidden target.

    :k C-u
    :snap -d 2s -e '5/5'

```terminal
session:                                                                                                               ┃
  5/5 | [C-r] repo: none                                                                                               ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
▌■ ui                                                                                                                  ┃
 ■ runner                                                                                                              ┃
 × alpha/first                              ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
 × alpha/alias                              ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
   alpha                                    ~/alpha                                                                    ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                                           delete [C-y] 2 sessions [C-g] cancel┃
```

Kill and restart the picker without cancelling its selection. Discovery restores
the staged state from the checkout, even when filtering to its other session.

    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :t kill-session -t ui (success)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth -r 'alpha*' --query alias; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 12 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :k C-p
    :snap -d 2s -e alpha/alias -e '2 sessions' -e '1 hidden' -e 'C-d. unstage'

```terminal
session: alias                                                                                                         ┃
  1/5 | [C-r] repo: none                                                                                               ┃
▌× alpha/alias                              ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] unstage, [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                 delete [C-y] 2 sessions (1 hidden) [C-g] cancel┃
```

Toggling through the alias removes the same marker. Cancellation removes it too.

    :k C-d
    :snap -d 2s -e alpha/alias -e 'C-d. delete'

```terminal
session: alias                                                                                                         ┃
  1/5 | [C-r] repo: none                                                                                               ┃
▌■ alpha/alias                              ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] delete, [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                                                                 ┃
```

    :$ test ! -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

Restage through the alias, then cancel. The ordinary delete hint should return
and the shared marker should disappear, just as it did when toggling off.

    :k C-d
    :settle -d 2s -e '2 sessions' -e '1 hidden' (settled)
    :k C-g
    :snap -d 2s -e alpha/alias -e 'C-d. delete'

```terminal
session: alias                                                                                                         ┃
  1/5 | [C-r] repo: none                                                                                               ┃
▌■ alpha/alias                              ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] delete, [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                                                                 ┃
```

    :$ test ! -f alpha.feature/.jj/.smth-pending-delete (exit: 0)

Confirming deletes the checkout once and closes both live sessions. Clearing
the query afterward should reveal only the three surviving entries, without
staged markers or a deletion footer.

    :k C-d
    :settle -d 2s -e '2 sessions' -e '1 hidden' (settled)
    :k C-y
    :$ sh -c 'i=0; while test -d alpha.feature || tmux has-session -t alpha/first 2>/dev/null || tmux has-session -t alpha/alias 2>/dev/null; do i=$((i+1)); test "$$i" -lt 100 || exit 1; sleep 0.05; done' (exit: 0)
    :settle -d 2s -e '0/3' (settled)

    :k C-u
    :snap -d 2s -e '3/3'

```terminal
session:                                                                                                               ┃
  3/3 | [C-r] repo: none                                                                                               ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
